  "release_notes": "New Features\n- Clip names: reorder the parts, turn each on or off, and add the game you were playing.\n- Clip editor: Trim for quick cuts, or the Full Editor for every track.\n- Full Editor: add video and audio tracks, and import videos, pictures and sound.\n- Move, trim, split and layer items, and set their volume, opacity, size and place on the video.\n- Move the clip along the timeline to fit an intro or outro.\n- Fades on items, tracks and the picture, and crossfade or slide transitions.\n- Assets deletes unused imports, or they go after 30 days.\n- Themes: Dark, Light, Halloween or Christmas, and save your own (Settings > UI Customization).\n\nImprovements\n- Game names prefer the fullscreen or focused app on screen (KDE, Windows).\n- No spaces in file names: Replay-2026-10-25-21-50-07-Deadlock.\n- The date is six dropdowns, in any order, each optional.\n- Between Parts is added for you (no hyphens needed), with Reset; Reset All resets every name option.\n- Exports include added tracks in the mix and .mkv.\n- Settings pages fit without scrolling on Windows.\n\nFixes\n- App tracks no longer miss the start of a clip, even while OBS restarts.\n- ClipEm's clip sound and Windows notifications no longer get a track or name the clip.\n- A clip opened before its tracks are saved gets them.\n- Clip names can't be just spaces.\n- A malformed OBS clip hotkey falls back to the default.\n- Setup's file check says when it lists only some problems.\n- Windows: restarts no longer wait on a closed launch.",
